** teaching philosophy
- based off my own training as a literary and queer scholar, and as a
  writing instructor for 6 years.
- techniques:
  - close reading as critical and creative: going into detail on
    individual examples, starting small.
  - writing as thinking: freewriting & papers; no substitute for
    critical work that happens when crafting a sentence; low stakes
    writing. 
  - all knowledge is contingent: from feminist and queer scholarship;
    acknowledging that "infinite vision is an illusion, a god trick"
    (Haraway 582).
    - incorporating critiques of intersectional femininism into every
